<algorithm id="fig001">
<meta>
<id>042.1</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title> Patients with Suspected Tachycardia: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0017-w0001-y.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Palpitations. Order 12-lead ECG. Pre-excitation present?</label>
<path target="cell-2">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-3">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-2">
<label>Suspect AVRT.</label>
<path target="cell-4"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-4">
<label>Refer to arrhythmia specialist.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Assess arrhythmia pattern by clinical history. History of syncope?</label>
<path target="cell-4">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-5">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Type of palpitations.</label>
<path target="cell-4">Sustained regular</path>
<path target="cell-6">Irregular palpitations</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Suspect atrial fibrillation, multifocal atrial tachycardia, or atrial flutter with with variable AV conduction.</label>
<path target="cell-7"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>Event monitor and follow-up.</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Blomstrom-Lundqvist C, Scheinman MM, Aliot EM, et al.; European Society of Cardiology Committee, NASPE-Heart Rhythm Society. ACC&#x002F;AHA&#x002F;ESC guidelines for the management of patients with supraventricular arrhythmias--executive summary. <em>J Am Coll Cardiol</em> 2003;<strong>42</strong>:1493-1531.<xref ref="pubmed14563598" resource="acc003" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
<algorithm id="fig002">
<meta>
<id>042.2</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title> Hemodynamically Stable Tachycardia: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0017-w0002-y.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-8">
<label>Hemodynamically stable regular tachycardia</label>
<path target="cell-12">Narrow QRS</path>
<path target="cell-18">Wide QRS, definite SVT</path>
<path target="cell-19">Wide QRS, VT or unknown</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>SVT</label>
<path target="cell-13"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Vagal maneuvers IV adenosine IV verapamil&#x002F;diltiazem IV beta blocker</label>
<path target="cell-14"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-14">
<label>Termination?</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-16">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Done</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>Persistent tachycardia with AV block</label>
<path target="cell-17"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-17">
<label>AV-nodal blocking agent plus one of the following: IV ibutilide (if 60 kg: 0.01 mg&#x002F;kg over 10 min; if &#x2265; 60 kg, 1 mg over 10 min), or IV procainamide, or IV flecainide (2 mg&#x002F;kg over 10 min), or overdrive pacing&#x002F;DC cardioversion</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-18">
<label>Pre-excitation?</label>
<path target="cell-12">No</path>
<path target="cell-17">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-19">
<label>Medical treatment or DC cardioversion</label>
<path target="cell-20">Medical</path>
<path target="cell-23">DC cardioversion</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-20">
<label>IV procainamide (30 mg&#x002F;min continuous infusion to max. of 17 mg&#x002F;kg) IV lidocaine (load 1 mg&#x002F;kg; repeat 0.5 mg&#x002F;kg q 10 min up to 3 mg&#x002F;kg; maintenance 1-4 mg&#x002F;min) IV amiodarone in patients with poor LV function (load 150 mg bolus; then 1 mg&#x002F;min for 6 hrs; then 0.5 mg&#x002F;min)</label>
<path target="cell-21"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-21">
<label>Termination?</label>
<path target="cell-22">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-23">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-22">
<label>Done</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-23">
<label>DC cardioversion</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Blomstrom-Lundqvist C, Scheinman MM, Aliot EM, et al. European Society of Cardiology Committee, NASPE-Heart Rhythm Society. ACC&#x002F;AHA&#x002F;ESC guidelines for the management of patients with supraventricular arrhythmias--executive summary. <em>J Am Coll Cardiol</em> 2003;<strong>42</strong>:1493-531.<xref ref="pubmed14563598" resource="acc003" />
</footnote>
<footnote>See text for dose.</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
<algorithm id="fig003">
<meta>
<id>042.3</id>
<supertype>AbCd</supertype>
<last_update>2007-09-13</last_update>
</meta>
<title> Paroxysmal Supraventricular Tachycardia: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0017-w0003-y.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-24">
<label>Patient with PSVT. Pre-excitation or severe symptoms?</label>
<path target="cell-25">No</path>
<path target="cell-26">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-25">
<label>Limiting symptoms?</label>
<path target="cell-27">No</path>
<path target="cell-28">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-27">
<label>No therapy</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-28">
<label>Drug therapy or RF ablation are treatment options</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-26">
<label>RF ablation. Successful?</label>
<path target="cell-29">No</path>
<path target="cell-30">Yes</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-29">
<label>Drug therapy</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-30">
<label>Done</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Adapted from Ferguson JD, DiMarco JP. Contemporary management of paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia. <em>Circulation</em> 2003;<strong>107</strong>:1096-1099.<xref ref="pubmed12615783" resource="acc001" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
</algorithm>
</algorithms>
